{"name":"Windy City","hex":"#88a3c2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Windy City","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Nickname for Chicago: a city in Illinois, United States.","Nickname for Wellington: the capital city of New Zealand."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Windy_City"}],"entries":[{"title":"Windy City (nickname)","blocks":[{"text":"The city of Chicago has been known by many nicknames, but it is most widely recognized as the \"Windy City\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/En-Chicago-CiteSourceWindyCityHistory01.gif/330px-En-Chicago-CiteSourceWindyCityHistory01.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windy_City_(nickname)"},{"title":"Baku","blocks":[{"text":"Baku is the capital and largest city of Azerbaijan, as well as the largest city on the Caspian Sea and in the Caucasus region. Baku is 28 metres (92 ft) below sea level, which makes it the lowest lying national capital in the world and the largest city in the world below sea level. Baku lies on the southern shore of the Absheron Peninsula, along the Bay of Baku. Baku's urban population is estimated at over two million people. Baku is the primate city of Azerbaijan. It is the sole metropolis in the country, and about 25% of all inhabitants of the country live in Baku's metropolitan area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Baku_Montage.jpg/330px-Baku_Montage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baku"},{"title":"City","blocks":[{"text":"A city is a human settlement of a substantial size. The term \"city\" has different meanings around the world and in some places the settlement can be very small. Even where the term is limited to larger settlements, there is no universally agreed definition of the lower numerical boundary for their size. In a more specific sense, a city can be defined as a permanent and densely populated place with administratively defined boundaries whose members work primarily on non-agricultural tasks. Cities generally have extensive systems for housing, transportation, sanitation, utilities, land use, production of goods, and communication. Their density facilitates interaction between people, government organizations, and businesses, sometimes benefiting different parties in the process, such as improving the efficiency of goods and service distribution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg/330px-Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Qobustan_inscription.jpg/500px-Qobustan_inscription.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Qobustan_inscription.jpg/1280px-Qobustan_inscription.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Qobustan_inscription.jpg/500px-Qobustan_inscription.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roman stone inscription in Gobustan dating back to AD 84–96","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQobustan_inscription.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/1541-Battle_in_the_war_between_Shah_Isma%27il_and_the_King_of_Shirvan-Shahnama-i-Isma%27il.jpg/500px-1541-Battle_in_the_war_between_Shah_Isma%27il_and_the_King_of_Shirvan-Shahnama-i-Isma%27il.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/1541-Battle_in_the_war_between_Shah_Isma